 Key Features of the UEFI ISO Builder
​Pure x86_64 UEFI Support: Includes standard 64-bit EFI binaries (BOOTX64.EFI) so modern PCs (like Dell Latitude 7370/7480 and modern UEFI-only motherboards) can detect and boot the USB drive.
​Predictable Interface Naming: Uses net.ifnames=0 biosdevname=0 boot options in GRUB so physical LAN ports reliably default to eth0 and wlan0, preserving your .88 IP assignment logic.
​Run-from-RAM Option (toram): Allows running the entire router engine in RAM so you can unplug the bootable USB flash drive once booted.
